      adverseEffects: ["Delayed active therapy, persistent intravascular source, and failure to search for metastatic infection increase mortality and relapse.", "Unnecessary prolonged broad therapy adds hepatic, interaction, line, cost, and resistance burden; premature step-down risks breakthrough infection."],
      contraindications: ["Do not step down based only on feeling better. Require a susceptible isolate, clinical stability, and documented bloodstream clearance.", "Do not start the 14-day count at admission or first dose. The uncomplicated-course clock follows clearance and symptom resolution."],
      nursingEssentials: ["Draw ordered repeat cultures daily or every other day until clearance, verify line/source plan, monitor hemodynamics and organ function, and make the first-negative-culture date visible in the care plan.", "Watch for new visual symptoms, murmur, embolic signs, focal bone/joint pain, neurologic change, persistent fever, or recurrent positive cultures and escalate for a deep focus."],
      interactions: ["Initial echinocandin therapy minimizes many CYP interactions; step-down fluconazole still requires warfarin, sulfonylurea, phenytoin, tacrolimus, QT, and renal-dose review.", "Total parenteral nutrition, broad antibiotics, abdominal surgery/leak, pancreatitis, neutropenia, dialysis access, and central lines are risk and source clues rather than drug interactions."],
      keyLabs: ["Serial blood cultures, species identification, azole susceptibility for relevant isolates, echinocandin susceptibility after prior exposure or for selected species, CBC, kidney/liver tests, and targeted imaging or echocardiography when indicated.", "Beta-D-glucan can support diagnosis in context but does not replace cultures, source control, or the clearance date."],
      nclexTraps: ["Candida in blood is clinically significant. Candida in urine, sputum, or a superficial swab may represent colonization and requires syndrome-specific interpretation.", "A negative culture is necessary but not sufficient: source control and exclusion of metastatic infection determine whether the course is truly uncomplicated."],
      sourceNote: "IDSA 2016 candidiasis guideline, still the current IDSA comprehensive management guideline at this release checkpoint.",
      tags: ["frontier-wave17", "candidemia", "source control", "step down", "blood cultures", "duration"]
